continue is a keyword whenever it is executed it will skip current iteration it will move on to the next iteration continue can be implemented in
only in the loops otherthan loops
if you're  writing continue keyword will get an compilation error saying misplaced continue.

Purpose of continue:
whenever we want to skip some part of iteration and to move on to the next iteration we can go for continue keyword.

eg:
  write a program to print 1 to 3 and 8 to 10 
  // Online C compiler to run C program online
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
   int a;
      for(a=1;a<=10;a++){
          if(a>3&&a<8){
              continue;
          }
          printf("%d ",a);
      }
    return 0;
}
output:
1 2 3 8 9 10 

